  "notes": "Warren J. Smith, Modern Lens Design, 2nd ed., Figure 16.21, p. 298. Book: EFL -5000, BFL 1000, NA 0.0087 (F/213.7), HFOV 1.00, VL 54.77, infinite conjugate. The book does not mark the stop; it is placed at surface 1, the plane entrance surface. The table gives thicknesses without sign; spaces after an odd number of reflections are entered negative, which reproduces the book's VL. Conic constants (kappa) and aspheric terms (ad, ae, af, ag on r^4, r^6, r^8, r^10) as in the book. The book decenters surface 2 by y = -32.000 (an off-axis aperture); it is entered as a coordinate break. As in the book (Afo 1000, MAG 5), an ideal lens of focal length 1000 follows the afocal system so it can be evaluated at a finite focus. EPD = EFL/F# (23.3973); the book's NA is a real marginal ray value that varies with the design's aberrations. The book's NA 0.0087 includes the off-axis aperture decenter, as in Fig 16.20. The three mirrors are not exactly afocal (focal length -4999.5 with the ideal lens), so the image lies 999.67 behind the ideal lens rather than 1000.",
